course: dictionary
lesson: 2587
title: Density: how tightly things are packed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Density tells you how much stuff is packed into a space. «Density means how much stuff is packed into the same space.» Imagine two boxes of the same size, one full of feathers and one full of bricks. The bricks are denser because more stuff fits into the same space.
explain: A dense thing is heavy for its size, so density decides whether things float or sink. Wood is less dense than water, so it floats. A stone is denser than water, so it sinks. Oil floats on water because it is less dense.
explain: Density can also describe people in a place. «Population density means how many people live on each square kilometre.» To find it, divide the number of people by the area. «Bangladesh has over 1,000» people per square kilometre, while «Australia has about 3», so Bangladesh has a much higher population density.
fact: Density means how much mass is packed into a certain amount of space.
fact: Dense things are heavy for their size.
fact: Population density is the number of people per square kilometre.
fact: To find population density, divide the number of people by the area.
fact: «High density» means tightly packed or crowded; «low density» means spread out.
exercise: «Density means how much stuff is packed into the same space.» What does density mean? | How tall something is | How much a thing weighs in grams only | *How much stuff is packed into a space | The colour of a thing
exercise: Wood floats on water. Why? | Wood is always heavier than water | Wood is denser than water | *Wood is less dense than water | Wood is always colder than water
exercise: Bangladesh has over 1,000 people per square kilometre and Australia has about 3. Which country has a higher population density? | *Bangladesh | Neither has any people | Both have the same | Australia
test: What is the correct way to find population density? | Subtract the area from the number of people | Add the number of people and the area | Multiply the number of people by the area | *Divide the number of people by the area
test: Which sentence describes high density? | Ten people live in a huge empty field | Two people live on a remote island | *Ten thousand people live packed into one small town | One tree grows in a wide desert
exam: Which object would sink in water, and why? | A cork, because it is light | *A steel nail, because steel is denser than water | A balloon filled with air, because it is full | A wooden spoon, because wood is dense
